Subject: [PATCH 2/7] feat: wire landing page to next-intl
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Extracts all user-facing landing page copy (hero, authority strip,
how-it-works cards, manifesto, scarcity, final CTA, footer) into
en.json under a new "landing" namespace, and replaces the hardcoded
English strings in src/app/page.tsx with useTranslations("landing")
calls. it.json gets these keys automatically via the Lara
auto-translate prebuild script on next build.

A few headings that used a manual <br/> for English line-wrapping now
flow as a single string — expected, since line breaks tied to English
wording don't hold up across languages.
